# Docker build-context hygiene (DEF-LANE-TRACKED-BINARY).
#
# Why this file exists: infra/Dockerfile.ahp is built with `context: .` and
# `COPY . .` (compose.yaml:99-101). Until 2026-11-10 the repository root also
# carried a TRACKED 28 MB ELF named `ahp`, so that build shipped a compiled binary
# of unknown provenance into its own context, and whichever `go build ./cmd/<name>`
# a lane happened to run last silently decided what the image contained.
#
# The patterns below exclude compiled outputs and local scratch from any
# repository-root build context. They never exclude a build input: go.mod, go.sum,
# cmd/, internal/, pkg/, infra/ and web/ (web/ is //go:embed'ed) all stay in, so
# the compile still has everything it needs.
#
# The mirrored .gitignore rules keep the same files out of `git status`; a leg in
# tests/hygiene/tracked_artifacts_test.go keeps the two lists from drifting.

# Root-level outputs of `go build ./cmd/<name>` with no -o.
/ahp
/ahp-agent
/ahp-deploy
/ahp-note-mcp
/artifact-parser
/as-runner
/compute-host
/state-consumer
/state-stand
/synthetic-authority

# Sanctioned build outputs and their provenance manifests: an image must be built
# from source or from an explicitly COPYed binary (scripts/build-candidate.sh),
# never from a whole output directory that happens to be lying around.
/bin/
/build-out/

# Local scratch that is never a build input.
/.git/
/.gocache/
/.ahp-evidence/
/coverage/
/infra/certs/
/node_modules/
